  "summary": "Held the entire 33-frame window without exiting. The thesis was intact throughout: price ran from entry to a peak of roughly +129pts favorable, and every pullback along the way (giveback 10-38% of the local swing) stayed well above zero and recovered into new highs, never threatening a round-trip to breakeven or negative territory. There was no sustained cluster of against-direction fires alongside a falling price floor -- KMDR/PROPP/HA against-signals fired intermittently but were consistently followed by continuation, not reversal. Next time I'd watch for the wrong-direction signature to look different: repeated against-fires PLUS price making lower highs AND breaching a prior swing low (not just a shallow retrace off a peak), or a giveback approaching 100% of the total trade amplitude rather than just the latest small leg."
